---
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About This Course">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-16">
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <div class="mb-16 text-center">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-neutral-900 lg:text-5xl dark:text-neutral-100">
        About This Course
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-xl text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">
        What happens when you ask AI to teach you about AI?
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Story Section -->
    <div class="prose prose-lg dark:prose-invert mx-auto">
      <div class="card mb-12 bg-gradient-to-br from-primary-50 to-accent-50 dark:from-primary-900/10 dark:to-accent-900/10">
        <h2 class="mt-0 text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">
          The Origin Story
        </h2>
        <p class="text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
          Like many developers, I watched AI explode into the mainstream with a mix of excitement and overwhelm. Every day brought new models, frameworks, and capabilities. The hype was deafening, but finding structured, honest education felt impossible.
        </p>
        <p class="text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
          So I had a thought: <em>What if I asked AI to build me the course I wish existed?</em>
        </p>
        <p class="text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
          Not a surface-level tutorial. Not marketing hype. A comprehensive training program that would take me from "I know AI exists" to "I can confidently integrate AI into my professional workflow."
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">
        The Experiment
      </h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
        This entire course was built through an AI-assisted workflow—essentially using AI to teach me how to use AI. The irony isn't lost on me.
      </p>

      <div class="card my-8 border-l-4 border-primary-600 bg-neutral-50 dark:border-primary-400 dark:bg-dark-surface">
        <p class="text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
          <strong>The Process:</strong>
        </p>
        <ol class="space-y-2 text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
          <li><strong>Ideation:</strong> I used Claude with extended thinking to explore what a comprehensive AI course should cover, digging deep into learning objectives, audience needs, and content structure.</li>
          <li><strong>Architecture:</strong> A specialized architecture agent transformed those ideas into detailed implementation plans—23 modules, interactive components, progressive learning paths.</li>
          <li><strong>Implementation:</strong> Multiple specialized agents built different aspects: content writing, code generation, quiz creation, diagram design, testing, and more.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>

      <p class="text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
        The result? You're looking at it. A complete, free, open-source course built almost entirely through structured AI collaboration.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">
        Why This Matters
      </h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
        This course is proof of concept. It demonstrates that:
      </p>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
        <li>AI can be a genuine <strong>force multiplier</strong> for building complex projects</li>
        <li>Structured workflows with specialized agents work <strong>better than generic prompting</strong></li>
        <li>AI excels at <strong>execution</strong> when given clear requirements and architecture</li>
        <li>The real skill is knowing <strong>what to ask for</strong> and <strong>how to direct the work</strong></li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">
        Course Philosophy
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <div class="card border-l-4 border-accent-600 dark:border-accent-400">
          <h3 class="mt-0 text-lg font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">
            🔧 AI is a Power Tool
          </h3>
          <p class="mb-0 text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
            Like a chainsaw, incredibly powerful but requires training to use safely. We teach proper operation, not just marketing copy.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card border-l-4 border-success-600 dark:border-success-400">
          <h3 class="mt-0 text-lg font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">
            🎯 Token Prediction, Not Magic
          </h3>
          <p class="mb-0 text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
            Modern LLMs are sophisticated pattern matchers, not reasoning engines. Understanding this limitation is crucial for effective use.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card border-l-4 border-warning-600 dark:border-warning-400">
          <h3 class="mt-0 text-lg font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">
            ⚖️ Honest About Controversy
          </h3>
          <p class="mb-0 text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
            We don't shy away from misalignment risks, safety concerns, environmental costs, or hype cycles. You deserve the full picture.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card border-l-4 border-primary-600 dark:border-primary-400">
          <h3 class="mt-0 text-lg font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">
            💼 Practical Over Theoretical
          </h3>
          <p class="mb-0 text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
            We balance accessible rigor with hands-on application. Theory matters, but only when it improves your practice.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">
        Who Am I?
      </h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
        A technical professional who wanted to truly understand AI beyond the hype. Someone who learns best by building. Someone who believes the best way to understand a technology is to use it to teach yourself about itself.
      </p>
      <p class="text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
        This course represents hundreds of hours of learning, experimentation, and iteration. I'm sharing it freely because I believe everyone in tech needs these skills, and education shouldn't be gatekept.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">
        What's Next?
      </h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
        This course will continue to evolve as AI technology advances. It's open source, community-driven, and built with the same AI tools it teaches.
      </p>
      <p class="text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
        Found a bug? See room for improvement? The GitHub repository is open for contributions. Let's make this resource better together.
      </p>

      <div class="card my-8 bg-gradient-to-r from-primary-50 to-accent-50 text-center dark:from-primary-900/20 dark:to-accent-900/20">
        <p class="text-lg font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">
          Ready to start learning?
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row sm:justify-center">
          <a
            href="/module/developer-mental-model"
            class="btn-primary inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2"
          >
            Begin Module 1
            <svg
              xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              stroke-width="2"
              stroke-linecap="round"
              stroke-linejoin="round"
              class="h-5 w-5"
            >
              <path d="M5 12h14" />
              <path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7" />
            </svg>
          </a>
          <a
            href="https://github.com/smartbeep4/trainer"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="btn-secondary inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2"
          >
            View on GitHub
            <svg
              xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              stroke-width="2"
              stroke-linecap="round"
              stroke-linejoin="round"
              class="h-5 w-5"
            >
              <path d="M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6" />
              <polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9" />
              <line x1="10" x2="21" y1="14" y2="3" />
            </svg>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-12 text-center text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">
        <p>
          <strong>License:</strong> Content is licensed under
          <a
            href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="text-primary-600 hover:underline dark:text-primary-400"
          >
            CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
          </a>. Code is MIT licensed.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
